# GFlowNet Project Structure

This codebase implements Generative Flow Networks (GFlowNets) in Julia. Key structure:

## Core Architecture

- **[src/GFlowNet.jl](mdc:src/GFlowNet.jl)**: Main module with exports
- **[src/core/](mdc:src/core/)**: Core algorithms and types
  - **[src/core/types.jl](mdc:src/core/types.jl)**: All core types and abstract interfaces
  - **[src/core/dag.jl](mdc:src/core/dag.jl)**: Directed Acyclic Graph operations
  - **[src/core/algorithms/](mdc:src/core/algorithms/)**: Core algorithmic components
- **[src/training/](mdc:src/training/)**: Training infrastructure 
- **[src/policies/](mdc:src/policies/)**: Neural network policy implementations
- **[examples/](mdc:examples/)**: Domain-specific applications

## High-Level Interface

Users should interact with GFlowNet through high-level functions:
- Use `GFlowNet.create_forward_policy()` instead of manual neural networks
- Use `GFlowNet.TrainingConfig()` and `GFlowNet.train_gflownet()` for training
- Use `GFlowNet.sample_trajectory()` for sampling

## Examples Pattern

Each example follows the same pattern:
1. Define domain-specific state/action types
2. Implement required interface functions (`state_to_features`, `is_applicable`, etc.)
3. Use high-level GFlowNet functions for model creation and training
4. Generate comprehensive results in `results/` directory

## Key Files for Reference

- **[examples/grid_world/grid_world.jl](mdc:examples/grid_world/grid_world.jl)**: Clean example using high-level interface
- **[src/training/trainer.jl](mdc:src/training/trainer.jl)**: High-level training functions
- **[src/core/algorithms/objectives.jl](mdc:src/core/algorithms/objectives.jl)**: Training objectives and neural network creators
